  vocab.json             ~/ocaml-bench-dashboard/schema/json/vocab.json
                         (generated from lib/schema/registry.ml)

Taken from a pinned REF, never the working copy: running-ng carries a dozen
feature branches, and a fixture captured from whichever one is checked out
silently changes what the tests mean. A checkout predating the input-size
ladder, for instance, has no `small_run` tag at all.

Why snapshots: the table tests must fail for one reason only -- a change in the
generator. Reading a live config would make them fail whenever someone edits a
tag or adds a benchmark, and a red test that is somebody else's edit is a test
people learn to ignore.

The live files are still covered: `make live` runs the same generation against
origin/adding-ocaml-support and pushes each config through running-ng's real
validate(). If that fails while `make test` passes, the base config moved and
these fixtures need refreshing.
